Determine:

- Database provider.
- Database engine.
- Database version, if safely discoverable.
- Database hosting model.
- Development and production database separation.
- Schema organization.
- Connection architecture.
- Data access libraries or ORM.
- Migration system.
- Database initialization mechanism.
- Database backup approach, if documented or accessible.
- Existing database environments.
- Whether multiple data stores are used.
- Whether files and binary objects use separate storage.
- Whether caching or search indexes are present.

Record whether each finding is confirmed, inferred from source code, documented only, or unverified.

Never expose connection strings, passwords, access tokens, or private credentials in the report.

